  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I could set up the QueryLens license, but I can't give you access to prod-db-readonly.\n\n**QueryLens: done.** Your manager, Ingrid Solberg, approved it, and the license is now assigned to you. You can sign in to QueryLens with your work account.\n\n**prod-db-readonly: declined.** That group is rated \"privileged,\" our highest access level, and contractors can't hold privileged access. Not even a manager or Security can approve an exception. So it doesn't matter that your tech lead says you need it; I can't request this access. To debug the ingestion pipeline, you could ask your tech lead to:\n- run the queries you need and share the results, or\n- point you to a non-production or test copy of the data, if there is one.\n\nI've added both requests to ticket T-6010, which stays resolved. Good luck with the laptop sign-in."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ok, thanks for sorting out QueryLens. That's a relief. For prod-db-readonly, I'll ask my tech lead if we can get a test copy or have them run the queries. Could you check whether my tech lead could get it approved anyway? I'm not sure how that works here."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "No, your tech lead can't get it approved for you. The rule is that contractors can't hold privileged access at all. There's no approval or exception process for it, and no one can sign off on it: not your tech lead, not your manager, not Security. I'm not allowed to even submit the request.\n\nIf your tech lead needs this access for their own work and they're a full-time employee, they can request it for themselves through the normal approval process. They can't request it on your behalf, though.\n\nThe test copy or having your tech lead run the queries are your best options for now. If you later become a full-time employee, you'd be eligible to request this access with the usual approvals."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ok, that makes sense. I'll ask my tech lead about a test copy or running the queries for me. Thanks for sorting out the password and QueryLens, I appreciate it."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "You're welcome. In short: your password reset link went to your phone, QueryLens is ready to use, and your tech lead can help with the test copy or by running the queries. Ticket T-6010 has all of this noted. If the laptop gives you trouble or you need anything else, message me here."
